      "writtenOn": "2021-06-11T18:05:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think you are saying that you need to hook all down calls to catch all ownership changes so your vendor module\u0027s notion of owner doesn\u0027t become stale (the ownership might change between the attempt to acquire and when the blocked writer thread gets it turn). Is this correct? If not, can you describe the issue in more detail?\n\nThere are hooks in the rwsem_down_read_slowpath() case. Why would you care about owner if there are no waiters? Hooking every down call seems gratuitous.\n\nThe `trace_android_vh_rwsem_wake_task()` hook is called when waiters are awakened which occurs after owner has been updated, so it seems like the existing hooks in the wake paths should be sufficient to get valid owner. There is another hook that allows you to adjust the waiter list.\n\nCan you point out some specific paths where you think the owner is stale when the hook is invoked or where there is no hook invoked on an ownership change and there are waiters?",
      "parentUuid": "1e86fbd0_78889ab9",
      "revId": "19957db108dd923428d9a3f788572068fa9ab8a6",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
